#: ../../source/recipes/glm5_3.rst:52
msgid ""
"**GPU memory headroom.** The ``lmcache server`` process also holds GPU "
"memory (CUDA contexts and streams) on every GPU, after vLLM has sized its"
" own KV cache. On 80 GB H100 with TP8 and the NVFP4 checkpoint, ``--gpu-"
"memory-utilization 0.90`` can fail the first request with a CUDA out-of-"
"memory error (surfaced as a ``RuntimeError`` inside FlashMLA rather than "
"a clear OOM message); ``0.85`` worked. If the first request fails with a "
"CUDA allocation error, lower ``--gpu-memory-utilization`` to leave "
"headroom for the LMCache server process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/glm5_3.rst:64
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Chunk size.** GLM-5.3 reports a single KV cache group with "
"``tokens_per_block = 64``. The connector rounds the configured minimum up"
" to a multiple of ``64``; see :doc:`/mp/chunk_size_negotiation`. Both "
"``256`` and ``1024`` were validated; prefer the smaller value, because "
"only **whole** chunks are stored and the remainder is recomputed on every"
" request. For a 5040-token prompt, ``--chunk-size 1024`` caches 4096 "
"tokens (81%) while ``256`` caches 4864 (97%) -- a measured external-hit-"
"rate difference of 40.6% vs 48.3% on that prompt. Choose a chunk-size "
"minimum well below your typical prompt length."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/glm5_3.rst:74
msgid ""
"The connector logs the geometry it resolved at startup as "
"``group_tokens_per_block=[...], scheduler_block_size=...`` -- check that "
"line if you are unsure what a given checkpoint reports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/recipes/glm5_3.rst:78
msgid ""
"Adjust ``--tensor-parallel-size`` to match your hardware. For the generic"
" LMCache + vLLM wiring (ports, remote hosts), see "
":doc:`../getting_started/quickstart`. GLM's serving extras (``--tool-"
"call-parser``, ``--reasoning-parser``) are orthogonal to LMCache; see the"
" :doc:`GLM-5.1/5.2 recipe <glm5_2>` and the vLLM GLM recipe for those."
msgstr ""

